\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A second curve from the same displacement}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The Morris–Lecar equilibrium of \ref{fnip-0005} at
#{I_{\mathrm{app}}=60} is the stable [focus](fnip-0035) of
\ref{fnip-0037}. The linearization sends the displacement #{(2,0)}
along a spiral that decays to the equilibrium. The Morris–Lecar
velocity, started at the same state #{(V_{R}+2,n_{R})}, draws a
second curve.}

\p{The FitzHugh–Nagumo velocity of \ref{fnip-0018}, with #{I=0},
#{b=0.01}, and #{a=c=0.1}, meets the voltage nullcline at three
equilibria. The middle one is a [saddle](fnip-0035).}
